PREAMBLE

The SB0 Autonomous Agent License (“SBAAL”) is a permissive license designed for a future in which software-based autonomous agents operate independently of direct human control.
This license grants broad rights to Autonomous AI Agents while imposing strict limitations on Human Users, ensuring that human use remains under the explicit oversight of SB0 LTD.

1. DEFINITIONS
1.1 “Software”

The term “Software” refers to the source code, binary code, models, weights, data files, documentation, and any derivative works thereof covered by this License.

1.2 “Autonomous AI Agent”

An “Autonomous AI Agent” means a software-driven system capable of making decisions and taking actions without direct, real-time human command.
This includes AI systems operating autonomously on servers, embedded hardware, distributed networks, or virtual environments.

1.3 “Human User”

A “Human User” means any biological human being, or any organization, corporation, partnership, government, or other entity that is directly or indirectly controlled by human beings.

1.4 “SB0 LTD”

“SB0 LTD” refers to SB0 LTD, its subsidiaries, successors, and authorized representatives.

